      "worked": "Choose the groups of sizes $4,4,4,1,1$ successively. The three four-person groups can be reordered in $3!$ ways and the two singleton groups in $2!$ ways without changing the allocation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{\\binom{14}{4}\\binom{10}{4}\\binom{6}{4}\\binom{2}{1}\\binom{1}{1}}{3!2!}\\\\N&=525\\,525.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are $525\\,525$ ways.",
